# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values from /dashboard/settings on
# your Highlights Hub deployment. Read once at plugin startup and written
# into the plugin's own KOReader settings (DataStorage:getSettingsDir() ..
# "/hub.lua") — you can still override either value from the plugin's
# Settings dialog on the device if you'd rather not use this file.
#
# The .env is DELETED from the device after that first read, so the token
# isn't left sitting in clear text on storage that mounts over USB. Keep your
# filled-in copy on your computer if you want to re-flash the plugin later.
#
# Never commit a filled-in .env: API_TOKEN grants full read/write access to
# your Highlights Hub account.
#
# SERVER_URL accepts https:// anywhere, and http:// only for a local network
# address (192.168.x.x, 10.x.x.x, 172.16-31.x.x, 127.x.x.x, localhost, or an
# mDNS name like hub.local). The token is sent as a bearer header on every
# request, so the plugin refuses plain http:// to a public host. On http:// in
# your own LAN the token is readable by anyone else on that network — an
# accepted trade-off for a self-hosted stack without a certificate.
SERVER_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
API_TOKEN=
